// Package scope registers exit actions (docs/spec/runtime.md, Exit
// actions). The Go body is runtime/v1's OnExit; its hidden argument, the
// caller's frame scope, is docs/spec/stdlib.md's Hidden arguments.

// OnExit registers body on the innermost enclosing function, as Go's defer
// does: it runs when that function returns, on every path, masked, and the
// blocks one call registered run last registered first. The block reads
// its variables when it runs. It is called directly, never as a value (an
// extern function is call-only).
extern go ergo.local/prototype/runtime/v1.OnExit func OnExit[R](body func() needs R) needs R
